# route: level=w6_l2b_coop difficulty=beginner players=2 ends=exit after=tally expect=wipes:0,x2_gates:1,unlocked:true,fight_ticks:1093..2185
# The Beginner two-stream route of Heart of the Mangrove in co-op (designer D6; recorded from
# build/d6/bot_w6_l2b_coop2.gd, P1|P2; club only, never S): up the trunk ahead of the rising tar, P2 one ledge behind
# P1; gate 'vent' - both into the vent room, both heave the boulder four tiles onto the two deadly tar vents (one hero
# alone only strains), both up over it and the step; the climb to the landing; then the co-op Old Mangrove (3 twin
# hits, then 2 on the stuck fist): P1 jumps from the lower root ledge onto the resting fist without Jump held and pins
# it, hops on it and clubs the face while P2, on the lower ledge under the hand's resting place (crouched while it
# sweeps), high-strikes the resting hand on his hop - the twin; in stage 3 P2 stands on the lower ledge just left of
# the stuck fist (the nearer hero: the knuckle armour turns to him) and P1 drops through the ledge's rotten hatch cells
# on the wrist side, clubbing the fist on the way down; the fire-starter and the team exit. No role waits 243 ticks
# without input (G33).
# Re-recorded in wf10 (bosses) with a copy of D6's bot (build/bosses10/bot_w6_l2b_coop3.gd: its hand / fist forecasts
# follow the new co-op rule) after the boss balance: fewer co-op hits (Beginner 3 + 2, Expert 4 + 3) and, in stage 1,
# hand and fist keep time (Mangrove._hand_waits_for_fist / _fist_waits_for_hand); fight 45-90 s pinned by fight_ticks.
# Re-recorded in wf10 by party with the same pilot (build/bosses10/bot_w6_l2b_coop3.gd): the rising view now keeps the
# highest footing of the pair 72 px under its top (LevelCamera.FOOTING_ROOM_PX), so the climb's wake-ups moved.
# Re-recorded in wf11 (levels; build/levels/bot_w6_l2b_coop.gd: the same pilot, whose P1 takes a step of the climb
# only while P2 stands still or climbs at most 4 rows under him): the footings of the pair are never more than six
# rows apart and the leash never takes P2 (three leash eggs before); under the ward of 'vent' (DESIGN G73, columns
# 0..28 over all rows) no digger of the chamber's left edge gives lift.
